<title>INDIA: Indian exports down 1.8 percent in December.</title>
<headline>Indian exports down 1.8 percent in December.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1997-01-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indian merchandise exports declined to $2.75 billion in December, down 1.8 percent from $2.80 billion in the same month in 1995, the government said on Friday.</p>
<p>    MERCHANDISE TRADE	 Dec 96    Dec 95</p>
<p>    Exports			2.75	2.80</p>
<p>    Imports			3.14	3.00</p>
<p>    Trade balance	     -0.39     -0.20</p>
<p>NOTE - Figures, in billions of dollars, may not add up due to rounding.</p>
<p>--------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>Indian merchandise exports grew 6.36 percent in April-March 1996 to $24.2 billion, the statement said.</p>
<p>    MERCHANDISE TRADE	 Apr-Dec 96   Apr-Dec 95</p>
<p>    Exports			 24.20	  22.76</p>
<p>    Imports			 27.45	  26.29</p>
<p>    Trade balance		 -3.25	  -3.53</p>
<p>NOTE - Figures, in billions of dollars, may not add up due to rounding.</p>
</text>
